# client — OPTIONAL .env. The zero-config defaults already pair this app with
# examples/server on :3001 (proxying /api/* and /x402/*), so you only need a
# .env to retarget or tune it:
#
#   # from the repo root:
#   cp examples/client/.env.example examples/client/.env
#   pnpm --filter @bnb-chain/mpp-example-client dev
#
# Delete .env (and restart dev) to return to the defaults.
# Note: chain preset / active tab persist in localStorage across visits —
# after switching .env, change the preset via the Chain dropdown or clear
# site data (the in-app Clear button only resets the tab's outputs).

# Vite proxy target for /api/* and /x402/* (examples/server listens on :3001).
# VITE_CHARGE_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001

# The protected mppx route to charge (examples/server serves /api/premium).
# VITE_DEFAULT_ENDPOINT=/api/premium

# The standalone x402 route the "x402 · Permit2" tab pays.
# VITE_X402_ENDPOINT=/x402/premium

# Default chain preset (see src/protocol/presets.ts). The $U presets surface
# the EIP-3009 `authorization` tab for a mode-3 (b402) server.
# ⚠️ testnet authorization settles currently fail upstream (ADR-0004 OQ2) —
# the testnet preset is a sign+submit demo; settlement works on mainnet only:
# VITE_DEFAULT_CHAIN_KEY=bsc-testnet-u
# ⚠️ MAINNET variant (REAL FUNDS): examples/server must run B402_CHAIN=bsc
# with mainnet credentials — then:
# VITE_DEFAULT_CHAIN_KEY=bsc-u

# Optional — your own RPCs (the public defaults rate-limit).
# VITE_BSC_TESTNET_RPC_URL=
# VITE_BSC_RPC_URL=
